  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ross reports:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "> I downloaded fedora-2.2.4-src.zip",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> unzipped into fedora-2.2.4-src",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> built with: ant installer",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> ran installer: java -jar fedora-2.2.4-installer.jar",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": ">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> Everything looked Ok and server came up with no problems. However, when I",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> tried to run some of the client command-line utilities I got \"/bin/sh^M",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> interpreter error\". Something either in the build or installer is changing",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> file formats to DOS format. The source files in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> fedora-2.2.4-src/src/sh/client and fedora-2.2.4-src/src/sh/server are in the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> correct unix format. However, the files copied into $FEDORA_HOME",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> fedora-2.2.4/client/bin and fedora-2.2.4/server/bin are in DOS file format.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> I fixed this by just running dos2unix utility to correct file formatting",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> issue.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
