  "description": "<p>Ross reports:</p>\n\n<p>&gt; I downloaded fedora-2.2.4-src.zip<br/>\n&gt; unzipped into fedora-2.2.4-src<br/>\n&gt; built with: ant installer<br/>\n&gt; ran installer: java -jar fedora-2.2.4-installer.jar<br/>\n&gt;<br/>\n&gt; Everything looked Ok and server came up with no problems. However, when I<br/>\n&gt; tried to run some of the client command-line utilities I got \"/bin/sh^M<br/>\n&gt; interpreter error\". Something either in the build or installer is changing<br/>\n&gt; file formats to DOS format. The source files in<br/>\n&gt; fedora-2.2.4-src/src/sh/client and fedora-2.2.4-src/src/sh/server are in the<br/>\n&gt; correct unix format. However, the files copied into $FEDORA_HOME<br/>\n&gt; fedora-2.2.4/client/bin and fedora-2.2.4/server/bin are in DOS file format.<br/>\n&gt; I fixed this by just running dos2unix utility to correct file formatting<br/>\n&gt; issue.</p>",
